                  to an odd-dimensional square vanishes (as does every
                  = succeed "-class);" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi MU
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} MU
              %li
                %p
                  with this, the bottom left rectangle exists, and it is a homotopy pushout by definition of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi M
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi 𝕊
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M \mathrm{U}/\mathbb{S}
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:BoundaryOperationViaPastingLaw"} (5)
              %li
                %p
                  hence the morphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathcolor => "magenta"}
                          %msup
                            %mi M
                            %mrow
                              %mn 2
                              %mi d
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \color{magenta} M^{2 d}
                  exists, and the resulting bottom middle square is a homotopy pushout, again by the
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting+law"} pasting law
              %li
                %p
                  Now the bottom right rectangle is defined to be a homotopy pushout, and thus looks as shown by the
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting+law"} pasting law
              %li
                %p
                  therefore the bottom right square exists, and it is a homotopy pushout by the
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting+law"} pasting law
            %p
