          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#ConnerFloyd66"}> Conner-Floyd 66, Theorem 16.2
            )
          %p
            The first step in the proof of
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:ToddClassesOnShortExactSequenceOfUFrBordismRings"} (8)
            is the observation (
            %a{:href => "#ConnerFloyd66"}> Conner-Floyd 66, p. 100-101
            ) that the representing map
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:InTermsOfHomotopyGroupsOfQuotientedThomSpace"} (1)
            for a
            = succeed "-manifold" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %mi fr
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (U,fr)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi M
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M^{2k}
            cobounding a
            = succeed "-manifold" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Fr
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Fr
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is given by the following
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+coherent+diagram"} homotopy
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting+diagram"} pasting diagram
            (see also at
            = succeed "):" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hopf+invariant"} Hopf invariant
                –
                %a{:href => "Hopf+invariant#InGeneralizedCohomology"} In generalized cohomology
          %div{:style => "margin: -20px 0px 20px 20px"}
            %figure{:style => "margin: 0 0 0 0"}
              %img{:alt => "homotopy pasting diagram exhibiting cobounding UFr-manifolds", :src => "/nlab/files/CoboundingUFrManifoldDiagrammatically.jpg", :width => "470px"}/
              %figcaption{:style => "text-align: center"}
                from
                %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/schreiber/show/Equivariant+Cohomotopy+and+Oriented+Cohomology+Theory"} SS21
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %div
            %p
              %strong>
                flavors of
                = succeed "/" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bordism+homology+theories"} bordism homology theories
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+cohomology+theories"} cobordism cohomology theories
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brown+representability+theorem"} representing
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+spectra"} Thom spectra
                and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+rings"} cobordism rings
              \:
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bordism+homology+theory"} bordism theory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \;
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M%28B%2Cf%29"} M(B,f)
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-bordism"}> B-bordism
              ):
            %ul
              %li
                %p
